-- title:
--   Lemma 3.3: the backward recursion under $\mathbb Q$ is increasing and computes $\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}[g(X_{t_n})\mid\mathcal F_{t_i}]$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $X$ is the recombining binomial tree of (3.11): nodes $x_{i,0}<\dots<x_{i,i}$ at time $t_i$ ($0\le i\le N$), up-probabilities $0<p^+_{i,j}<1$; $\varphi_{t_1},\dots,\varphi_{t_N}$ are distortion functions and $\varphi_{t_0}(p)=p$; $G_{i,j}=\mathbb P(X_{t_i}\ge x_{i,j})$, $G_{i,i+1}=0$; $q^\pm_{i,j}$ and $\mathbb Q$ are given by (3.13) and (3.15); and condition (3.14) holds.
--
--   Let $g\in\mathcal I$ and $0<n\le N$. Define $u_n(x):=g(x)$ and, for $i=n-1,\dots,0$,
--   $$
--   u_i(x_{i,j}):=q^+_{i,j}\,u_{i+1}(x_{i+1,j+1})+q^-_{i,j}\,u_{i+1}(x_{i+1,j}),\qquad j=0,\dots,i. \tag{3.16}
--   $$
--   Then, for every $0\le i\le n$:
--
--   1. $u_i$ is increasing: $u_i(x_{i,j})\le u_i(x_{i,j'})$ for $0\le j\le j'\le i$;
--   2. $\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}[g(X_{t_n})\mid\mathcal F_{t_i}]=u_i(X_{t_i})$.
--
--   The recursion is a discrete backward equation; the monotonicity of $u_i$ is what lets the inner conditional expectation be fed back into the class $\mathcal I$ when the tower property is checked.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Since $x_{i,0}<\dots<x_{i,i}$, monotonicity of $u_i$ on the nodes is monotonicity in $j$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a Markov process X on an abstract filtered probability space with transition law (3.11) and the filtration F = F^X it generates → the canonical path space Fin N → Bool (true = up) with path weights ∏ p^±, and X_{t_i}(ω) = x_{i, number of up-moves before i}; reason: every quantity in the statement depends only on the law of X and on F^X; the same instances
--   - encoding: times 0 = t_0 < ⋯ < t_N → time indices 0, …, N (Φ(t_i, t_n, x; p) is Φ i n x p, φ_{t_n} is φ n); reason: the times enter only as labels
--   - encoding: the assumption φ_0(p) := p → phiExt φ 0 = id built into the definitions; the value φ 0 of the given family is ignored; reason: the same convention, without a hypothesis on φ 0
--   - encoding: conditioning on F_{t_i} (resp. σ(X_{t_i})) and identities between random variables → conditioning on the atom of F_{t_i} containing ω (resp. on the event {X_{t_i} = X_{t_i}(ω)}), identities stated at every path ω; reason: F_{t_i} = σ(X_{t_0}, …, X_{t_i}) is generated by these atoms, and every path has positive probability, so almost-sure identities are identities at every path
--   - reading: u_i for i = n − 1, …, 0, with u_n := g → both clauses stated for 0 ≤ i ≤ n; reason: at i = n they are the statements about u_n = g, which the induction starts from
-- source:
--   Ma–Wong–Zhang, Time-consistent conditional expectation under probability distortion, arXiv:1809.08262v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.08262v5, Lemma 3.3, eq. (3.16), p.13

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Distortion
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Tree
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Dynamic

open MeasureTheory Set

namespace DistortedCondExp

/-- **Lemma 3.3** (Ma–Wong–Zhang, arXiv:1809.08262v5, p.13). Assume (3.14) holds and `g ∈ ℐ`. For
`0 < n ≤ N`, define `u_n(x) := g(x)` and, for `i = n − 1, …, 0`,
`u_i(x_{i,j}) := q⁺_{i,j} u_{i+1}(x_{i+1,j+1}) + q⁻_{i,j} u_{i+1}(x_{i+1,j})`, `j = 0, …, i` (3.16).
Then `u_i` is increasing and `𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | F_{t_i}] = u_i(X_{t_i})`.

**Formalization Note** `uLemma x q g n i j` is `u_i(x_{i,j})`. Since `x_{i,0} < ⋯ < x_{i,i}`, "`u_i`
is increasing" on the nodes `{x_{i,j}}` is monotonicity in `j ∈ {0, …, i}`. Both clauses are
stated for `0 ≤ i ≤ n` (at `i = n` they are the statements about `u_n = g`).
`𝔼^ℚ[· | F_{t_i}]` at the path `ω` is the `ℚ`-conditional expectation given the atom
`histAtom i ω` of `F_{t_i}`, and `u_i(X_{t_i}(ω)) = u_i(x_{i, lev i ω})`. -/
theorem lemma_3_3 (N : ℕ) (x p : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (φ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (htree : IsBinomialTree N x p) (hφ : ∀ n, 1 ≤ n → n ≤ N → IsDistortion (φ n))
    (h314 : Cond314 N x p φ)
    (g : ℝ → ℝ) (hg : InI g) (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) (hnN : n ≤ N) :
    (∀ i, i ≤ n → ∀ j j', j ≤ j' → j' ≤ i →
      uLemma x (qPlus N x p φ) g n i j ≤ uLemma x (qPlus N x p φ) g n i j') ∧
    (∀ i, i ≤ n → ∀ ω : Path N,
      cexp (qPlus N x p φ) (fun ω' => g (X x n ω')) (histAtom i ω) =
        uLemma x (qPlus N x p φ) g n i (lev i ω)) := by sorry

end DistortedCondExp
